  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Polda Banten has officially opened a criminal investigation into the factory fire at PT Fonusa Agung Mulia in Cikande, Serang.",
    "Search and rescue efforts remain ongoing, with 26 body bags recovered while approximately 30 workers are still reported as missing.",
    "Local officials and labor organizations are calling for a thorough safety audit and the implementation of stricter industrial standards."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire recently struck the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in the Cikande district of Serang, Banten, resulting in multiple casualties and missing persons. While search teams continue to recover victims, with 16 individuals already identified, concerns regarding industrial safety protocols have intensified. Reports suggest the incident may have been triggered by an electrical short circuit in an air conditioning unit, leading to staff being trapped inside the facility. In response to the tragedy, Polda Banten has elevated the status of the case to a formal investigation. Meanwhile, local government officials and representatives from the labor sector are demanding mandatory workplace safety evaluations for all industrial sites in Serang to prevent further fatalities. Affected families are currently receiving support through BPJS Ketenagakerjaan compensation programs as recovery and identification processes proceed.",
